  <static seed="227" source="Contrib/DMOI/0-Introduction_and_Preliminaries/0_3-Sets/0_3_4.pg">
    <statement><p>Let <m>A  = {\left\{2,4,5,6,7\right\}}</m> and 
<m>B = {\left\{2,4,5,6,8\right\}}.</m>
Find a set of largest possible size that is a subset of both <m>A  \text{ and } B \text{.}</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left\{2,4,5,6\right\}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>The set of largest size that is a subset of both <m>A  \text{ and } B</m> is the <em>intersection</em> of <m>A  \text{ and } B \text{,}</m> <m>A \cap B = {\left\{2,4,5,6\right\}}\text{.}</m></p>
</solution>
